The interface in src/shared/store/read/context.ts (currently `:49-55`) becomes exactly:
```ts
export interface ToolContext {
  readonly reader: GraphReader;
  readonly cursor: CursorFacade;
  readonly log: Logger;
  readonly now: () => Date;
  readonly config: AppConfig;
  /**
   * The byte size of the `graph.db` this reader opened, recorded by the composition root when the
   * file was fingerprinted (before `openReader`) and never re-measured: a publish renames a new
   * file over the path, so a `stat` taken in a handler can describe a generation this handle
   * cannot serve. `null` when no file was served; absent on a hand-written fake written before
   * the field existed, which is why it is optional.
   */
  readonly dbSizeBytes?: number | null;
}
```
Optional, so the eight hand-written `ToolContext` literals under `tests/` (e.g. tests/read-files.test.ts:714-720, tests/tools-status.test.ts:299-308) keep type-checking; `number | null` so "no file served" (`null`, the unreadable-reader context at src/index.ts:977) is distinguishable from "not recorded" (`undefined`). Keep the import list unchanged (`AppConfig`, `CursorExpectation/CursorPayload/CursorResult`, `Logger`, `GraphReader`) and import nothing from `src/tools/**` or `src/index.ts`. Do not make the field required, do not add another member, do not edit any other file.

Signature (src/index.ts:407):
```ts
function buildContext(
  config: AppConfig,
  reader: GraphReader,
  dbSizeBytes: number | null,
): ToolContext {
  return { reader, cursor: createCursors({ key: config.cursorKey, repoId: canonicalRoot(config.repoRoot) }), log, now: () => new Date(), config, dbSizeBytes };
}
```
Call sites, each passing the fingerprint that belongs to the handle being served:
- `:472` in `openStore`: `context: buildContext(config, reader, fingerprint.size)` — the same local `fingerprint` const the `ready` Store returns; it is non-null there because `fingerprint === null || fingerprint.size === 0` already returned `absent` above.
- `:521` in `refreshStore` (the `replacement`): `context: buildContext(config, reader, now.size)` — `now` is the fingerprint taken before `openReader`, the same value stamped on the replacement.
- `:978` in `openFor`:
```ts
    const reader = store.kind === "ready" ? store.context.reader : unreadableReader();
    // The size belongs to the handle this call serves: the print `refreshStore` recorded (or kept)
    // for the file it opened, never a stat of the path.
    const dbSizeBytes = store.kind === "ready" ? (store.fingerprint?.size ?? null) : null;
    return { store, context: buildContext(repoConfig, reader, dbSizeBytes) };
```
Do NOT: add a member to `Store` or `FileFingerprint`; stat the file after opening it; change the pre-open fingerprint order or its comment (`:436-441`); change `sameFile` or the refusal path; add a syscall to the hot path; edit `src/tools/status/handler.ts` or any test. `src/index.ts:1198` (`{ ...store.context, log: scopedLog(name) }`) inherits the field with no edit — leave it alone.
